module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreEmbedding.SegrePresentation
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Basic

/-!
# The standard charts of `Proj` of the Segre product, and that they cover

The one thing Stacks Tag 01WD still owes is an isomorphism between `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj` of the
Segre product and the fibre product of two projective spaces; see
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreClosedImmersion.absoluteSegre_of_projSegreIso`.  The proof of that
isomorphism is a gluing argument over the loci where one generator `x_i * y_j` is invertible.
This file exhibits those loci as affine opens, names the ring each is the spectrum of, and proves
that they **cover**.

## What is proved, and the route

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.genSub R X Y p` is the generator `x_i * y_j` as an element
  of the Segre product, and `genSub_mem_grading_one` places it in degree one.  Degree one is
  positive, which is the only thing the chart results need.

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.isAffineOpen_basicOpen_genSub`: the locus
  `D₊(x_i y_j) ⊆ Proj 𝒮` is an affine open.  This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen` at a homogeneous element of positive degree.

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.basicOpenGenSubIsoSpec`: that locus is the spectrum of
  `HomogeneousLocalization.Away (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y) (genSub R X Y p)`,
  the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of the Segre product at `x_i y_j`.  This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpenIsoSpec`.  That ring is computed, and shown to be a tensor
  product of two polynomial rings, in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SegreEmbedding/SegreChartRing.lean`.

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.iSup_basicOpen_genSub_eq_top`: **the loci cover**.  This
  is `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top` applied to
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.irrelevant_le_span_genSub`, the containment of the
  irrelevant ideal of the Segre product in the ideal generated by the `x_i y_j`, and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.affineOpenCoverGenSub` packages it as an affine open
  cover indexed by the pairs.

  The containment is the subalgebra-level form of
  `Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.exists_list_prod_eq_monomial`, which says a monomial of degree
  `d` in each group of variables is a product of `d` generators, so for `d` positive it has a
  generator as a factor.  Two transports are involved and are done in two separate steps.
  `HomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal_irrelevant_le` reduces the homogeneous-ideal containment to a
  degreewise plain-ideal one, which is what removes the mismatch between the shape
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top` wants and the shape
  `HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant_le` gives.  Then
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.gradePiece_le_map_span` does the ambient-to-subalgebra
  transport: the sum over the support of a polynomial is taken in the ambient polynomial ring,
  where `MvPolynomial.as_sum` is available, and the target is the image of the ideal under the
  inclusion of the subalgebra, so each monomial contributes a constant times a nonempty product
  of generators — `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts.genSubProd` — which lies in the ideal by
  `genSubProd_cons_mem_span`.  Injectivity of the inclusion then moves the conclusion back inside
  the subalgebra, in `mem_span_genSub_of_mem_grading`.

## Implementation notes

The grading of the Segre product is taken as an ordinary instance binder, not supplied here:
`Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.gradingGradedAlgebra` is a definition rather than an instance, and
a local instance introduced in a statement does not survive into its proof.  Consumers supply the
canonical grading in the body of a definition, as
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SegreEmbedding/SegreClosedImmersion.lean` does.

`genSubProd` is a product over a `List`, matching the shape in which
`exists_list_prod_eq_monomial` produces its witness; a nonempty list is a `cons`, which is what
makes the ideal membership one application of `Ideal.mul_mem_right`.

## What is not done

The chart data and the cover are here; the geometry of the comparison is not.  No morphism between
`Proj` of the Segre product and a product of projective spaces is constructed anywhere, in either
direction.  Specifically, and in the order a proof would need them, after the cover proved here
and the chart ring computed in the companion file:

* the comparison of the affine chart of the product of two projective spaces with the spectrum of
  that tensor product, for which `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSpecIso` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι` are the tools;
* the compatibility of all of these on the overlaps
  `D₊(x_i y_j) ∩ D₊(x_k y_l) = D₊(x_i y_j x_k y_l)`, for which
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.pullbackAwayιIso` is the available tool, and the gluing itself.
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts

universe v u

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (X Y : Type v)
  [GradedAlgebra (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y)]

/-- The generator `x_i * y_j`, as an element of the Segre product. -/
public noncomputable def genSub (p : X × Y) :
    Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.segre R X Y :=
  ⟨Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.gen R X Y p,
    Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.gen_mem_segre R X Y p⟩

omit [GradedAlgebra (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y)] in
/-- The generator `x_i * y_j` lies in degree one of the Segre product. -/
public theorem genSub_mem_grading_one (p : X × Y) :
    genSub R X Y p ∈ Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y 1 :=
  Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.gen_mem R X Y p

/-- The locus where a generator `x_i * y_j` is invertible is an affine open of `Proj` of the Segre
product. -/
public theorem isAffineOpen_basicOpen_genSub (p : X × Y) :
    IsAffineOpen (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen
      (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y) (genSub R X Y p)) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen _ _ (genSub_mem_grading_one R X Y p) one_pos

/-- **The standard chart.**  The locus where `x_i * y_j` is invertible is the spectrum of the
degree-zero homogeneous localisation of the Segre product at `x_i * y_j`.  That ring is computed
in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SegreEmbedding/SegreChartRing.lean`, where it is identified
with the tensor product of the corresponding affine charts of the two projective spaces. -/
public noncomputable def basicOpenGenSubIsoSpec (p : X × Y) :
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen
        (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y) (genSub R X Y p)).toScheme ≅
      Spec (CommRingCat.of (HomogeneousLocalization.Away
        (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y) (genSub R X Y p))) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpenIsoSpec _ _ (genSub_mem_grading_one R X Y p) one_pos

/-! ### The standard charts cover `Proj` of the Segre product -/

open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- A product of generators, as an element of the Segre product. -/
public noncomputable def genSubProd (l : List (X × Y)) : segre R X Y :=
  (l.map (genSub R X Y)).prod

omit [GradedAlgebra (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y)] in
open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- A product of generators of the Segre product is, in the ambient polynomial ring, the
corresponding product of the polynomials `x_i * y_j`. -/
public theorem val_genSubProd (l : List (X × Y)) :
    ((genSubProd R X Y l : segre R X Y) : MvPolynomial (X ⊕ Y) R) =
      (l.map (gen R X Y)).prod := by
  rw [show ((genSubProd R X Y l : segre R X Y) : MvPolynomial (X ⊕ Y) R) =
      (segre R X Y).val (genSubProd R X Y l) from rfl, genSubProd, map_list_prod,
    List.map_map]
  rfl

omit [GradedAlgebra (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y)] in
open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- A nonempty product of generators lies in the ideal they generate. -/
public theorem genSubProd_cons_mem_span (p : X × Y) (l : List (X × Y)) :
    genSubProd R X Y (p :: l) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range (genSub R X Y)) := by
  rw [genSubProd, List.map_cons, List.prod_cons]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨p, rfl⟩)

omit [GradedAlgebra (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y)] in
open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- **The coupling identity, transported to the ideal generated by the generators.**  Every
element of the degree-`d` piece of the Segre product, `d` positive, is a polynomial that lies in
the image of the ideal generated by the `x_i * y_j`.

This is the ambient-ring form: the sum over the support of the polynomial is taken in the
polynomial ring, where `MvPolynomial.as_sum` is available, and each monomial is a unit scalar
times a product of `d` generators by
`Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.exists_list_prod_eq_monomial`, the list being nonempty because
`d` is positive. -/
public theorem gradePiece_le_map_span (d : ℕ) (hd : 0 < d) :
    gradePiece R X Y d ≤
      Submodule.map (segre R X Y).val.toLinearMap
        (Submodule.restrictScalars R (Ideal.span (Set.range (genSub R X Y)))) := by
  classical
  intro a ha
  have key : ∑ α ∈ a.support,
      (MvPolynomial.monomial α (a.coeff α) : MvPolynomial (X ⊕ Y) R) ∈
        Submodule.map (segre R X Y).val.toLinearMap
          (Submodule.restrictScalars R (Ideal.span (Set.range (genSub R X Y)))) := by
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun α hα => ?_
    have hne := MvPolynomial.mem_support_iff.mp hα
    obtain ⟨l, hlen, hl⟩ :=
      exists_list_prod_eq_monomial R X Y d α (ha.1 hne) (ha.2 hne)
    rcases l with _ | ⟨q, l'⟩
    · rw [List.length_nil] at hlen
      omega
    refine ⟨algebraMap R (segre R X Y) (a.coeff α) *
      genSubProd R X Y (q :: l'), Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _
        (genSubProd_cons_mem_span R X Y q l'), ?_⟩
    rw [AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply, map_mul, AlgHom.commutes, Subalgebra.coe_val,
      val_genSubProd, ← hl, MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq, MvPolynomial.C_mul_monomial, mul_one]
  rwa [← a.as_sum] at key

omit [GradedAlgebra (Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct.grading R X Y)] in
open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- Every element of a positive-degree component of the Segre product lies in the ideal generated
by the `x_i * y_j`. -/
public theorem mem_span_genSub_of_mem_grading {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    {s : segre R X Y} (hs : s ∈ grading R X Y d) :
    s ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range (genSub R X Y)) := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hts⟩ := gradePiece_le_map_span R X Y d hd hs
  exact Subtype.ext hts ▸ ht

open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- **The generators span the irrelevant ideal.**  This is the hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top`: the homogeneous-ideal containment is reduced to a
degreewise plain-ideal one by `HomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal_irrelevant_le`. -/
public theorem irrelevant_le_span_genSub :
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (grading R X Y)).toIdeal ≤
      Ideal.span (Set.range (genSub R X Y)) :=
  (HomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal_irrelevant_le _).mpr fun _ hi _ hs =>
    mem_span_genSub_of_mem_grading R X Y hi hs

open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- **The standard charts cover.**  The loci where a generator `x_i * y_j` is invertible cover
`Proj` of the Segre product. -/
public theorem iSup_basicOpen_genSub_eq_top :
    ⨆ p : X × Y, AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (grading R X Y) (genSub R X Y p) = ⊤ :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top _ _ (irrelevant_le_span_genSub R X Y)

open Stacks.RingTheory.SegreProduct in
/-- **The standard affine open cover of `Proj` of the Segre product**, indexed by the pairs
`(i, j)`, the chart at `(i, j)` being the spectrum of the degree-zero homogeneous localisation at
`x_i * y_j`. -/
public noncomputable def affineOpenCoverGenSub :
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (grading R X Y)).AffineOpenCover :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.affineOpenCoverOfIrrelevantLESpan _ (genSub R X Y)
    (m := fun _ => 1) (fun p => genSub_mem_grading_one R X Y p) (fun _ => one_pos)
    (irrelevant_le_span_genSub R X Y)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreCharts

end
